My only concern here is using callback as the dependency might cause the effect being triggered on every render, if an inline anonymous function is passed. In that case all the metrics will always get re-reported again.

I think a better way is put the callback in a ref, and get rid of the effect dependency:

```suggestion
  const callbackRef = useRef(callback)
  useEffect(() => callbackRef.current = callback)

  useEffect(() => {
    const handler = metric => callbackRef.current(metric)

    metrics.forEach((metric) => handler(metric))

    webVitalsCallbacks.add(handler)
    return () => {
      webVitalsCallbacks.delete(handler)
    }
  }, [])
```

Like I mentioned [here](https://github.com/vercel/next.js/pull/28769#discussion_r707125931), we have to use a closure to wrap the latest reference of the callback in a new function first, then put it inside the set. Otherwise it still calls the initial callback when new metrics are received in the future.

```suggestion
  useEffect(() => {
    const reportMetric =
      metric => callbackRef.current(metric)

    if (metrics.length) {
      metrics.forEach(reportMetric)
    }

    webVitalsCallbacks.add(reportMetric)
    return () => {
      webVitalsCallbacks.delete(reportMetric)
    }
  }, [])
```

There's an even bigger problem too: this doesn't support [Strict Effects](https://github.com/reactwg/react-18/discussions/18) -- it'll resend every metric. I'd suggest just doing something like this:

```ts
const lastIndexRef = useRef(0)

useEffect(() => {
  const reportMetric = metric => {
    callback(metric)
    lastIndexRef.current = i
  }
  for (let i = lastIndexRef.current; i < metrics.length; i++) {
    reportMetric(metrics[i])
  }
  
  webVitalsCallbacks.add(reportMetric)
  return () => {
    webVitalsCallbacks.delete(reportMetric)
  }
}, [callback])
```

The callback itself doesn't need to be stored in a ref, since this effect is called whenever `callback` changes. Instead, we store the last metric index we sent in a ref, that way we'll only report a metric to a given component instance at most one time, regardless of the callback identity.

